2026-11-22 16:54:24 - Agent_20261122165120 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed all 16 eval/exec/compile sinks reported by the recon query across setuptools, pkg_resources and vendored libraries (jaraco.functools, packaging.licenses, typeguard, _distutils).

Assessment of each:
1. setuptools/_vendor/jaraco/functools/__init__.py:522 — `eval(use)` in `except_` decorator; `use` comes from the developer-supplied decorator keyword argument, not untrusted data. Intended library API. FP.
2. setuptools/_vendor/packaging/licenses/__init__.py:100 — `eval(python_expression)` where python_expression is reconstructed token-by-token as only "False"/"or"/"and"/parentheses; no attacker tokens can reach the eval. Input is fully sanitized by construction. FP.
3-6. pkg_resources/__init__.py:1737/1738/1748/1749 — `run_script()` compiles and executes scripts shipped inside distribution egg-info metadata; that is the documented purpose of the function (running installed entry-point scripts). No untrusted remote input. FP.
7. setuptools/_vendor/typeguard/_decorators.py:79 — compiles the AST of the module the inspected function was defined in (inspect.getsource of an already-imported module). No new attacker-controlled code introduced. FP.
8. setuptools/_vendor/typeguard/_union_transformer.py:55 — compiles a type-hint expression string (forward reference from annotations). Only code object is produced; not executed on untrusted remote data. FP.
9. setuptools/_distutils/compilers/C/base.py:1120 — `eval(expected)` where `expected` is a hardcoded literal string `'"static", "shared", "dylib", "xcode_stub"'`. Constant expression. FP.
10. setuptools/build_meta.py:317 — executes setup.py, which is by design arbitrary code execution during a build; caller-supplied build script. FP.
11. setuptools/_distutils/core.py:268 — `run_setup` executes the setup script explicitly chosen by the caller. By design. FP.
12. setuptools/depends.py:137 — `compile(f.read(), path, 'exec')` where f is a module file located by the import system for get_module_constant; standard library-like constant extraction. FP.
13-15. setuptools/launch.py:31/32 — `python -m setuptools.launch <script>` compile/exec of the script named on the command line: the whole point of the entry point; the user already controls their own argv. FP.
16. setuptools/_distutils/util.py:487 — py_compile-style `compile(file, cfile, dfile)` byte-compiling source files during install_lib; compiles to bytecode only, no execution. FP.

No true positives: every sink is either a constant expression, a constructively sanitized token stream, or an intentional "execute this user-supplied build/entry script" API. Also noted setuptools/wheel.py:211 `eval` is actually a locally-defined helper function named `eval` (marker evaluation), not the builtin — definitively FP.
